---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Labs" description="Research labs: Space Instrumentation and Space Weather, and data sources of the HelioFísica y Clima Espacial USACH group.">

<section>
  <span class="section-title">Labs</span>
  <h1>Research laboratories</h1>
  <p class="lead">Two research laboratories and the data sources we use for our science.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">
    <h3>Space Instrumentation Lab</h3>
    <p>Ground-based magnetometer network (SAMBA chain, Chile). Deployment, calibration, and maintenance of magnetometers for monitoring geomagnetic field variations. Antarctic field campaigns (Chilean Scientific Antarctic Expedition 47, 2011). Comparative magnetometer performance analysis (Universidad Adventista de Chile deployment, 2025). Collaboration with MACCS, THEMIS GBO, and CARISMA networks.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">
    <h3>Space Weather Lab</h3>
    <p>Real-time monitoring of solar activity and its influence on the Earth's magnetosphere. Development of deep learning predictive models for magnetic perturbations, geomagnetically induced currents (GIC), and relativistic electron dynamics. The national space weather platform (FONDEF IDEA I+D) integrates solar wind, magnetic field, and particle data for early warnings. Collaboration with Universidad Adventista de Chile.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <span class="section-title">Data sources</span>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Satellites</h3>
      <p>Van Allen Probes (MagEIS, REPT, EMFISIS, EFW) · THEMIS (SPEDAS) · GOES · OMNI</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Ground magnetometers</h3>
      <p>SAMBA · MACCS · THEMIS GBO · CARISMA · SuperDARN</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Tools</h3>
      <p>Python (SciPy, Pandas, Numpy, Matplotlib, SpacePy) · TensorFlow-Keras · PyTorch · Scikit-learn</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

</Layout>